<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carl Gustaf Emil Mannerheim</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1867–1951</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Gustaf Mannerheim</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carl Gustaf Emil Mannerheim was a Finnish soldier and statesman who served as a general in the Russian imperial army before leading the White forces to victory in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finnish-civil-war">Finnish Civil War</a> of 1918. He was regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finland">Finland</a> in 1918–1919, commanded the Finnish army in the Winter War and the Continuation War against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, became a marshal, and was president of Finland from 1944 to 1946.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carl-gustaf-emil-mannerheim.jpg" alt="Carl Gustaf Emil Mannerheim" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: sa-kuva · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mannerheim1940.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
